  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tackling the illegal trade of tigers, rhinos and other endangered species of willdife in Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is funding year 1 of a 1-year grant. Education for Nature-Vietnam (ENV) is a leading conservation organization in Vietnam, actively and strategically working with government agencies, the general public, and other conservation partner organizations to stop illegal hunting and illegal wildlife trade in Vietnam. The purpose of this project is to continue to strengthen enforcement, improve and reshape policies and laws, and mobilize public support to combat wildlife trafficking in Vietnam. The project has the following objectives: (1) Strengthen policy and laws to help protect tigers, rhinos and other endangered species; (2) Combat illegal tiger trade and disrupt criminal networks engaged in smuggling and trade of tigers, rhinos, and other endangered wildlife; and, (3) Reduce consumer demand for wildlife and wildlife product with a focus on high priority species including tigers, rhinos (horn), and pangolins, and mobilize public action in efforts to stop wildlife crime and reduce consumption of wildlife.</narrative>
  </description>
